# Old Google Sites URLs -> new pages. 301 so search engines move the ranking
# across instead of dropping the old pages.
#
# Targets are extensionless on purpose. Cloudflare Pages serves /directors from
# directors.html and 301s /directors.html back to /directors. Pointing a rule
# at the .html form therefore costs an extra hop — and where the old URL and
# the clean URL are the same string it is an infinite loop.
#
# That is why /directors and /contact have NO rule here: Pages already serves
# both natively, and adding one broke them.

/home                       /                          301

/directors/mr-pinoux        /director-mr-pinoux        301
/directors/ariles-de-tizi   /director-ariles-de-tizi   301
/directors/chris-cuseo      /director-chris-cuseo      301
/directors/lordface         /director-lordface         301

/randomz                    /backstage                 301
/randomz/2016-fabric        /backstage-fabric-london   301
/randomz/elle-bts           /backstage-elle-bts        301

# Catch anything else that lived under those two sections.
/directors/*                /directors                 301
/randomz/*                  /backstage                 301
